<title>BELGIUM: Sub-Saharan Africa only AEA region with less Apr c.</title>
<headline>Sub-Saharan Africa only AEA region with less Apr c.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air cargo traffic rose in all Association of European Airlines (AEA) regions in April from year ago levels except for Europe-Sub Saharan Africa. The overall total climbed 2.6 percent to 1,969.3 million revenue freight tonne kilometres (RFTK).</p>
<p>AEA said from its Brussels headquarters that this sector fell by 4.7 percent to 147.5 m RTKF. The largest increase was experienced in the Mid Atlantic trade which increased by 19.6 percent to 107.3m RTKF.</p>
<p>  Region				Million     Percent Change</p>
<p>					    RTKF	vs Apr '96</p>
<p>  Geographical Europe		 81.3	up    8.6</p>
<p>  Europe-N Africa/M East	    92.2	up    8.6</p>
<p>  North Atlantic		     692.2	up    1.3</p>
<p>  Europe-Far East/Australasia    735.8	up    1.9</p>
<p>  Europe-Sub Saharan Africa	147.5	down  4.7</p>
<p>  South Atlantic		     112.7	up    2.5</p>
<p>  Mid Atlantic			 107.3	up   19.6</p>
<p>  Total longhaul		   1,795.8	up    2.0</p>
<p>  Total international	    1,969.3	up    2.6</p>
<p>*These figures relate to the international scheduled services of AEA member airlines.</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.comtraffic rose</p>
</text>
